{"stream": "process_log", "ts": "2026-08-26T12:44:37.308032+00:00", "agent": "email_agent", "objectId": "533967041217", "run_id": "306054b059d14804a585c1dd50eb12e9", "step": 5, "event": "profile", "object_id": "533967041217", "email_id": "bychowdary05@gmail.com", "first_name": "Mahitha", "last_name": "Naganaboina", "employee_id": "E00021", "job_title": "Vice President", "company": "M1 Finance", "industry": "FINANCIAL_SERVICES", "company_id": "C0021", "company_size_revenue": "4.7", "location": "", "linkedin_url": "", "phone": "+1 (469) 731-0345", "probability": 21, "email_status": "DELIVERED", "lead_context": "M1 Finance is a Chicago-based fintech platform with assets under management rising to over $12\u201312.5B by late 2025/early 2026 and a user base exceeding one million, built around automated features like Auto-Invest and Dynamic Rebalancing that automatically allocate and rebalance portfolio positions. The platform also has an AI assistant in beta, meaning AI-driven decisioning is already embedded \u2014 or actively being embedded \u2014 in customer-facing workflows. This puts M1 squarely in the territory the post addresses: SR 26-2 excludes generative AI and agentic AI from its formal scope because these technologies are novel and rapidly evolving, but as one analysis puts it, a gap in supervisory guidance is not a gap in risk \u2014 if a generative AI use case fails, the loss, the customer harm, and the reputational cost are unchanged by the fact that the framework no longer names it. M1 operates as a broker-dealer and registered investment adviser, making it subject to safety-and-soundness oversight regardless of the SR 26-2 carve-out. The post's argument \u2014 that institutions should engineer governance controls (audit trails, human-in-the-loop review, least-privilege access) as a native property of AI systems rather than assembling evidence for an exam \u2014 is directly relevant to M1 as it scales its AI assistant and automated portfolio logic ahead of the agencies' forthcoming RFI on AI-specific model risk. The one question a rep could open with: **As M1 expands its AI assistant and automated decisioning features, how is the team currently thinking about demonstrating control over those systems to examiners who will ask behavioral questions rather than check a compliance box?**", "company_website": "https://m1.com", "company_about": "Fintech platform offering commission-free automated investing, high-yield cash accounts, and margin loans, letting users build customizable brokerage, retirement, and crypto portfolios.", "industry_group": "Investment / Wealth Management (Automated Investing)", "missing_pointers": ["location", "linkedin_url"]}
