{"stream": "process_log", "ts": "2026-08-26T13:21:37.477772+00:00", "agent": "email_agent", "objectId": "533963448020", "run_id": "bf5448cecb7643c08fdf70e975ef2ab2", "step": 5, "event": "profile", "object_id": "533963448020", "email_id": "mahesh.p@tekninjas.com", "first_name": "Mahesh", "last_name": "Puliganti", "employee_id": "E00017", "job_title": "President", "company": "Axiom Law", "industry": "HEALTHCARE", "company_id": "C0017", "company_size_revenue": "6.6", "location": "", "linkedin_url": "", "phone": "+1 (469) 884-7673", "probability": 2, "email_status": "DELIVERED", "lead_context": "Axiom Law sits at the exact intersection where this post's governance argument lands hardest. Axiom is a global alternative legal services provider delivering on-demand legal talent, secondments, and AI-enabled legal services to in-house legal departments. Its healthcare practice serves hospitals, health systems, physician practices, pharmaceutical companies, and medical device manufacturers, with deep knowledge in Medicare and Medicaid reimbursement and health information technology. That client base is now swimming in the exact regulatory turbulence the post describes: states are enacting laws in 2026 that govern insurers' use of AI in prior authorization and claims decisions, increase transparency requirements, and require human oversight for adverse determinations. Critically, CMS rules now require a clinician \u2014 not AI alone \u2014 to make coverage calls, which is precisely the human-in-the-loop design the post calls \"defensible.\" Axiom has been actively commercializing its own AI position: its Legora partnership, now a year old, is delivering results specifically across healthcare clients, and Axiom now offers 850+ AI-experienced legal professionals. Yet its own 2025 AI study found only 20% of legal departments achieve AI maturity, creating dangerous competency gaps. As President, Puliganti shapes how Axiom positions its AI-enabled talent to healthcare GCs navigating this governance minefield \u2014 making the post's framework for auditable, human-owned AI decisions directly relevant to Axiom's go-to-market story. **Opening question:** When Axiom's healthcare clients ask how to design AI workflows that survive congressional or state-level scrutiny, what governance safeguards are they most urgently asking for help implementing?", "company_website": "https://www.axiomlaw.com", "company_about": "Global alternative legal services provider delivering on-demand legal talent, secondments, and AI-enabled legal services to in-house legal departments via a network of vetted lawyers.", "industry_group": "Alternative Legal Services (ALSP)", "missing_pointers": ["location", "linkedin_url"]}
