{"stream": "process_log", "ts": "2026-08-26T14:45:20.974240+00:00", "agent": "email_agent", "objectId": "533965249249", "run_id": "5b025c6c12a7422db5c9738218eac0d5", "step": 5, "event": "profile", "object_id": "533965249249", "email_id": "austin.t@tekninjas.com", "first_name": "Austin", "last_name": "Terry", "employee_id": "E00019", "job_title": "Managing Director", "company": "Cedar", "industry": "HEALTHCARE", "company_id": "C0019", "company_size_revenue": "11.5", "location": "", "linkedin_url": "", "phone": "+1 (469) 699-8559", "probability": 2, "email_status": "DELIVERED", "lead_context": "Cedar is the performance engine for healthcare financial experience, built on AI to solve the growing complexity of patient financial engagement \u2014 its platform unifies billing, payments, coverage, and support into a single solution powered by more than a billion patient interactions. That scale of real-time data flow makes API reliability and observability a genuine operational concern. Cedar recently launched Kora, its AI voice agent, to automate patient interactions, and expanded Cedar Intelligence capabilities to help providers personalize patient billing experiences at scale. Each of these AI-driven product surfaces depends on robust, well-instrumented APIs \u2014 exactly the territory covered in our FastAPI logging guide. Logging is critical for understanding and debugging FastAPI apps in production; when things go wrong, logs are the best starting point, covering both request logs and application logs. Built-in data masking is a particularly relevant detail for Cedar given healthcare data sensitivity. The rep should note that Cedar is actively scaling AI product surface area while managing sensitive patient financial data \u2014 observability gaps carry real compliance and reliability risk here. **Opening question:** As Cedar scales AI-powered products like Kora and Cedar Intelligence, how is your engineering team currently handling API-level visibility and log correlation across those services in production?", "company_website": "https://www.cedar.com", "company_about": "Healthcare financial platform that unifies billing, payments, insurance coverage, and patient support to improve collections and the patient payment experience.", "industry_group": "Healthcare Payments / RCM", "missing_pointers": ["location", "linkedin_url"]}
