{"stream": "process_log", "ts": "2026-08-26T14:46:49.051356+00:00", "agent": "email_agent", "objectId": "533990588137", "run_id": "62234f7887ba46bcb534839f7d308080", "step": 5, "event": "profile", "object_id": "533990588137", "email_id": "govardhan.t@tekninjas.com", "first_name": "Govardhan", "last_name": "Terli", "employee_id": "E00010", "job_title": "Managing Director", "company": "Health Catalyst", "industry": "HEALTHCARE", "company_id": "C0010", "company_size_revenue": "11.5", "location": "", "linkedin_url": "", "phone": "+1 (469) 312-6842", "probability": 2, "email_status": "DELIVERED", "lead_context": "Health Catalyst is a publicly traded (Nasdaq: HCAT) healthcare intelligence company in the middle of a deliberate strategic reset. In Q1 2026, management took what it called \"the first decisive step toward transforming our operating model,\" describing it as \"a strategic reset designed to build a more focused, durable Health Catalyst.\" Concretely, that strategy centres on the Ignite platform, health information exchange deployments, and AI-driven automation, while moving away from lower-margin services work. Ignite is a scalable healthcare data and analytics platform that unifies clinical, financial, and claims data into a standardised model, enabling self-service analytics, embedded AI, and faster enterprise decision-making. It ships with prebuilt connectors for 40+ healthcare systems and native support for FHIR, HL7, and OMOP \u2014 meaning Health Catalyst's engineering teams are managing a dense ecosystem of APIs carrying highly sensitive patient data in production. This is exactly where the Apitally FastAPI logging guide lands: logging is critical for understanding and debugging FastAPI apps in production, and for APIs specifically it splits into request logs \u2014 recording individual requests and responses \u2014 and application logs containing detailed messages from application code. By default, tools like Apitally don't capture sensitive data, making them suitable for environments with strict privacy requirements \u2014 a non-trivial differentiator for a HITRUST-certified company serving health systems. A good opening question for the rep: *As Health Catalyst doubles down on the Ignite platform and its AI co-pilot, how is your engineering team currently handling request-level observability and log correlation across the APIs that move clinical and financial data between health system clients?*", "company_website": "https://www.healthcatalyst.com", "company_about": "Healthcare data-and-analytics company that unifies data and applies AI-powered insights to drive measurable clinical, financial, and operational improvement for provider organizations.", "industry_group": "Healthcare Data & Analytics", "missing_pointers": ["location", "linkedin_url"]}
