{"stream": "process_log", "ts": "2026-08-26T15:11:07.428761+00:00", "agent": "email_agent", "objectId": "534035230400", "run_id": "b1168e195b4240b48742fd8fd79ca833", "step": 5, "event": "profile", "object_id": "534035230400", "email_id": "naveen.p@tekninjas.com", "first_name": "Kodanda", "last_name": "Naveen", "employee_id": "E00016", "job_title": "Managing Director", "company": "Innovaccer", "industry": "HEALTHCARE", "company_id": "C0016", "company_size_revenue": "11.5", "location": "", "linkedin_url": "", "phone": "+1 (469) 850-0314", "probability": 2, "email_status": "DELIVERED", "lead_context": "Innovaccer is a high-velocity healthcare AI platform company that has been expanding its product surface aggressively in 2026. It recently launched Atlas, a Population Health Operating System that orchestrates data, AI, and care delivery into a unified experience to track longitudinal outcomes across all payment models. It has also launched Galaxy UM for AI-powered utilization management automation, acquired CaduceusHealth to advance revenue cycle autonomy, and launched Gravity AI for infusion access workflows. Black Book Research recognized Innovaccer as a 2026 top-ranked vendor in both AI-Powered Revenue Cycle Autonomy and Population Health Data Integration, Activation & Analytics. Each of these new products and integrations is almost certainly built on or exposed through internal APIs \u2014 and Innovaccer's own research finds that fragmented data environments are now the primary constraint on scaling AI impact in healthcare. The post we published addresses exactly the operational visibility problem this creates: API logging breaks down into request logs and application logs, and ideally both are correlated so each log record is linked to the specific API request \u2014 critical for debugging failures in clinical or financial workflows where data errors carry real patient and revenue consequences. By default, tools like Apitally don't capture sensitive data, making them suitable for environments with strict privacy requirements \u2014 a meaningful differentiator for a HIPAA-governed platform like Innovaccer's. A good opening question for the rep: *As Innovaccer scales Atlas and its agentic workflows across clinical, operational, and financial APIs, what does your current observability and request logging setup look like when something breaks in a production API?*", "company_website": "https://innovaccer.com", "company_about": "Offers an AI-driven healthcare cloud that unifies data and deploys agents across clinical, operational, and financial workflows including population health, care management, and revenue cycle.", "industry_group": "Healthcare Data Platform / Population Health", "missing_pointers": ["location", "linkedin_url"]}
