{"stream": "process_log", "ts": "2026-08-26T15:12:14.647624+00:00", "agent": "email_agent", "objectId": "533990588137", "run_id": "284a8e42b99a4c7b81af449e1901ea04", "step": 5, "event": "profile", "object_id": "533990588137", "email_id": "govardhan.t@tekninjas.com", "first_name": "Govardhan", "last_name": "Terli", "employee_id": "E00010", "job_title": "Managing Director", "company": "Health Catalyst", "industry": "HEALTHCARE", "company_id": "C0010", "company_size_revenue": "11.5", "location": "", "linkedin_url": "", "phone": "+1 (469) 312-6842", "probability": 2, "email_status": "DELIVERED", "lead_context": "**lead_context note for Govardhan Terli, Managing Director \u2014 Health Catalyst**\n\n---\n\nHealth Catalyst recently sold its Vitalware mid-revenue-cycle business to Med-Metrix for $147 million, with plans to use the proceeds to repay outstanding debt and sharpen its focus on AI, analytics, and its core technology platform. That platform \u2014 Ignite\u2122 \u2014 unifies clinical, financial, and claims data into a standardized model, enabling self-service analytics, embedded AI, and faster enterprise decision making \u2014 is now the company's primary growth vehicle, relied upon by more than 1,100 organizations worldwide. Delivering on that scale means Health Catalyst's engineering teams are running many interconnected APIs in production. Ignite introduced built-in observability and intelligent alerting to detect issues proactively, with the ability to define custom thresholds based on what truly matters to their pipelines. Our FastAPI logging guide speaks directly to this need: for APIs, logging breaks down into request logs and application logs, and ideally both are correlated so each log record is linked to the API request \u2014 exactly the kind of visibility a platform serving 1,100+ healthcare clients in regulated environments must get right. By default, Apitally doesn't capture any sensitive data, making it suitable for environments with strict privacy requirements \u2014 a natural fit for a HIPAA-sensitive company. A good opening question for a rep: *As Health Catalyst doubles down on Ignite and expands its AI-integrated offerings, how are your engineering teams currently handling API observability and log correlation across production services?*", "company_website": "https://www.healthcatalyst.com", "company_about": "Healthcare data-and-analytics company that unifies data and applies AI-powered insights to drive measurable clinical, financial, and operational improvement for provider organizations.", "industry_group": "Healthcare Data & Analytics", "missing_pointers": ["location", "linkedin_url"]}
