{"stream": "process_log", "ts": "2026-08-26T15:13:11.424289+00:00", "agent": "email_agent", "objectId": "534035230400", "run_id": "a1c5df51579f4bd68d8b0c5ba05feefc", "step": 5, "event": "profile", "object_id": "534035230400", "email_id": "naveen.p@tekninjas.com", "first_name": "Kodanda", "last_name": "Naveen", "employee_id": "E00016", "job_title": "Managing Director", "company": "Innovaccer", "industry": "HEALTHCARE", "company_id": "C0016", "company_size_revenue": "11.5", "location": "", "linkedin_url": "", "phone": "+1 (469) 850-0314", "probability": 2, "email_status": "DELIVERED", "lead_context": "Innovaccer is a fast-moving healthcare AI platform company whose core product stack centers on unifying clinical, operational, and financial data to power agentic AI workflows. The company has committed $250 million to expand its AI agent platform, which automates workflows across areas like prior authorization, revenue cycle management, and population health. Its Gravity infrastructure layer ingests and normalizes data from across an enterprise \u2014 including EHR systems, claims, pharmacy, labs, remote monitoring, and social determinants of health \u2014 and makes it available to the application and agent layers above it. Innovaccer was just named a Leader in the inaugural 2026 Gartner Magic Quadrant for Healthcare Provider Industry Cloud Platforms, arriving at a moment when most health systems and payers are still struggling to move AI beyond pilots and into enterprise workflows. This growth trajectory means its engineering teams are almost certainly running complex, high-throughput Python-based APIs \u2014 exactly the context where our FastAPI logging guide lands. Production API logging is critical for understanding and debugging FastAPI apps, and for APIs specifically, that breaks down into request logs (recording individual API requests and responses) and application logs (containing detailed messages from application code). Built-in data masking is also a non-trivial concern for a company handling sensitive patient data at enterprise scale. A strong opening question for a first conversation: *As Innovaccer scales agentic AI workflows across more clinical and financial APIs, how is the engineering team currently handling request-level observability and log correlation in production?*", "company_website": "https://innovaccer.com", "company_about": "Offers an AI-driven healthcare cloud that unifies data and deploys agents across clinical, operational, and financial workflows including population health, care management, and revenue cycle.", "industry_group": "Healthcare Data Platform / Population Health", "missing_pointers": ["location", "linkedin_url"]}
