{"stream": "process_log", "ts": "2026-08-26T20:11:32.569095+00:00", "agent": "email_agent", "objectId": "533990588137", "run_id": "db3bfe3cbad54838b8ffb7f5fade0df1", "step": 5, "event": "profile", "object_id": "533990588137", "email_id": "govardhan.t@tekninjas.com", "first_name": "Govardhan", "last_name": "Terli", "employee_id": "E00010", "job_title": "Managing Director", "company": "", "industry": "", "company_id": "", "company_size_revenue": "", "location": "", "linkedin_url": "", "phone": "+1 (469) 312-6842", "probability": 2, "email_status": "DELIVERED", "lead_context": "**lead_context \u2014 Govardhan Terli, Managing Director, Health Catalyst**\n\nHealth Catalyst is actively migrating its core data and analytics capabilities from its legacy Data Operating System (DOS) to the cloud-based Ignite\u2122 platform. Ignite streams data from over 300 source templates and exposes pre-built standard APIs, meaning the engineering teams supporting this transition are building and operating a growing surface area of FastAPI-style Python services that connect clinical, financial, and operational data to downstream consumers. Analysts cite the DOS-to-Ignite transition as a key driver of current operational complexity and risk, which implies the platform engineering org is under real pressure to keep those APIs reliable and debuggable in production. Our post \u2014 a complete guide to FastAPI logging, covering structured output, request/response correlation, and tools like Apitally \u2014 lands squarely on that pain: logging is critical for understanding and debugging FastAPI apps in production, and when things go wrong, logs are usually the first place engineers look. Data masking and sensitive-data controls add a HIPAA-relevant angle that is directly material for a healthcare data platform. A strong opening question for the rep: *As Health Catalyst scales Ignite's API layer across more health system clients, how is the engineering team currently handling structured logging and request traceability across those production services?*", "company_website": "", "company_about": "", "industry_group": "", "missing_pointers": ["external_company_id", "industry", "company_size_revenue", "location", "linkedin_url"]}
